From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:45:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 105/111] ASoC: tlv320adc3xxx: TDM slots, clocking from BCLK, a
 shared reset line

From lidar-mainline by LeagueRaINi (GPL-2.0, commit db8242a), backported
to 6.12 for the MT8516 Echos (ADR 0031). The remove() hunk was redone by
hand against 6.12's, which still checks for MCLK.

The MT8516 Echos put several TLV320ADC3101s on one TDM bus (two on the
Echo Dot (3rd gen), four on the Echo Plus (2nd gen)), clocked by the
AFE's BCLK, with one reset line for all of them:

- set_tdm_slot: each codec drives its own slots;
- without MCLK the codec runs from BCLK, as clock consumer;
- "reset-gpios" goes through the reset framework when it can be shared;
  a shared line is only released, and each codec is reset in software.
